<BaseLayout title="Privacy" description="How AI Amigos browser tools, local storage, optional sync, exports, analytics, and feed retrieval protect visitor inputs."><div class="shell reading"><p class="eyebrow">Privacy by architecture</p><h1>Your working data stays private by default.</h1><p>The practice workspace runs locally in your browser first. AI Amigos does not receive project answers, imported notes, artifacts, evaluations, or generated outputs unless you deliberately submit a sanitized proof pack for editorial review.</p><h2>Local projects and optional sync</h2><p>Projects, stage history, and exports are saved in versioned browser storage. An optional account and sync layer may be enabled later; it is separate from the local-first path and is governed by the project membership and retention rules shown at sign-in. Use Reset or delete a project to remove the local copy; clearing site data also removes it.</p><h2>Model runs and keys</h2><p>Manual notes work without an account or model. If the optional BYOK model path is enabled, your credential is sent only for one authenticated run through an ephemeral server-side proxy. It is not stored, logged, placed in a URL, or returned to the browser after the run. Do not paste regulated or confidential records.</p><h2>Exports and sharing</h2><p>Markdown, JSON, CSV, copy, print, and proof-pack export happen only when you choose them. “Share this tool” copies a stable tool or playbook page link and never adds your inputs or private result to the URL. A public playbook contains the sanitized summary, method, evidence links, limitations, and outcomes you explicitly submit—not your private artifact contents.</p><h2>Anonymous measurement</h2><p>Umami is inactive unless a verified site ID is configured. If enabled, AI Amigos sends only an anonymous event name and resource ID—for example, tool completion, template copy, guide-to-tool click, or playbook fork. Form fields and generated outputs are never included.</p><h2>News feeds</h2><p>Approved RSS or Atom sources are retrieved during the site build, not by your browser. Only sanitized metadata and original links are displayed. A source without a valid response or cached snapshot fails closed.</p><h2>Newsletter and contact</h2><p>Subscription collection is inactive until a provider and matching retention notice are configured. Contact actions open your email application; AI Amigos does not host a contact-form database.</p><h2>External destinations</h2><p>External source, newsletter, and newspaper links have their own privacy terms. Review them before entering information.</p></div></BaseLayout>
